  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young men and women, including in the most vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, have acquired skills that are in demand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This initiative seeks to strengthen the employability and resilience of young Afghan men and women, with particular focus on those from vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, including women and persons with disabilities. It promotes the development of market-relevant skills and fosters   inclusive, sustainable, and lifelong learning opportunities. Working in close collaboration with national constituents, most notably the Afghanistan Chamber of Commerce and Investment (ACCI), the Afghanistan Women&#x2019;s Chamber of Commerce and Industry (AWCCI), and other employers&#x2019; organizations and their provincial chapters, the initiative support skills identification, curriculum development, and work-based learning programmes in micro-, small-, and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs). The initiative also supports inclusive skills development initiatives designed and implemented by employers&#x2019; organizations with targeted support for women and persons with disabilities, skills recognition programmes that enhances employability and facilitate labour market integration. In partnership with the International Training Centre of the ILO (ITCILO), the initiative also provides technical assistance to develop digital tools that identify skills in demand, accessible in local languages, and digitalize selected training modules to expand outreach and accessibility. By conducting skills needs assessments in selected industrial parks and target regions, and supporting employers in designing climate-resilient skills programmes, the initiative helps align education and training systems with real employment demand and environmental sustainability needs. Through these integrated efforts, the initiative contributes to Afghanistan&#x2019;s broader objectives of poverty reduction, economic recovery, climate change adaptation, and sustainable development even amid challenging socio-political conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
